@page "/mana-base"

<PageTitle>Mana Base Analyzer - Card Game Calculator</PageTitle>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Mana Base Analyzer</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-6" Color="Color.Secondary">
    Calculate the probability of hitting your land drops on curve.
</MudText>

<MudExpansionPanels Class="mb-6" MultiExpansion="true">
    <MudExpansionPanel Text="Theory & Math">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The Mana Base Analyzer models land draws using the hypergeometric distribution.
            By turn \(T\), a player has seen \(h + T\) cards in total — an opening hand of \(h\) cards
            plus one draw per turn. The probability of having drawn at least \(L\) lands by turn \(T\) is:
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(X \geq L) = \sum_{i=L}^{\min(\ell,\; h+T)} \frac{\binom{\ell}{i}\,\binom{N-\ell}{h+T-i}}{\binom{N}{h+T}} $$
        </div>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mt-2 mb-1">Miss land drop</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            A player <em>misses their \(T\)-th land drop</em> when they have seen fewer than \(T\) lands
            after \(h + T\) cards — that is, when \(P(X \geq T)\) is not met:
        </MudText>
        <div class="my-3">
            $$ P(\text{miss land drop at turn } T) = 1 - P(X \geq T) $$
        </div>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mt-4 mb-2">Parameters</MudText>
        <MudText>\(N\) — deck size</MudText>
        <MudText>\(\ell\) — number of lands in the deck</MudText>
        <MudText>\(h\) — opening hand size</MudText>
        <MudText>\(L\) — land threshold (at least \(L\) lands)</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">\(T\) — turn number</MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mt-4 mb-2">Assumptions &amp; Simplifications</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            The following simplifications are in effect. Verify that they are acceptable for your use case
            before relying on the results.
        </MudText>
        <ul style="padding-left: 1.5rem;" class="mb-4">
            <li><strong>No mulligans</strong> — the opening hand is kept as-is. Mulligans reduce effective hand size and alter how many lands a player sees early. For mulligan-aware estimates, use the Mulligan &amp; Looting Calculator.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>Exactly one draw per turn</strong> — cards seen accumulate linearly as \(h + T\). Looting, cycling, scry, fetch lands, and any other mechanism that draws or filters additional cards are not modeled.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>No fetchlands or land tutors</strong> — all cards have equal probability of being a land. Fetch lands, Cultivate, and similar effects that selectively add lands to hand or play are not modeled.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>Lands produce unrestricted mana</strong> — color requirements are not modeled. All lands are treated as functionally equivalent basic lands.</li>
            <li class="mt-2"><strong>Perfect shuffle</strong> — the deck is treated as uniformly randomly ordered. Imperfect shuffling that causes clumping or bias is not modeled.</li>
        </ul>
    </MudExpansionPanel>

    <MudExpansionPanel Text="How to Use">
        <MudText Class="mb-3">
            Set the deck parameters and press <strong>Calculate</strong>. The chart plots the probability
            of having seen at least 1–5 lands at each turn; the table gives the exact figures alongside
            the miss-land-drop probability for each turn.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle2" Class="mb-2">Example — Hitting the 4th Land Drop in Standard</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-2">
            Your 60-card Standard deck runs 24 lands. What is the probability of having at least 4 lands
            available by turn 4, assuming you keep your opening hand of 7?
        </MudText>
        <ol style="padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            <li>Deck Size: <strong>60</strong></li>
            <li>Lands in Deck: <strong>24</strong></li>
            <li>Opening Hand Size: <strong>7</strong></li>
            <li>Turns to Show: <strong>5</strong> (or more)</li>
        </ol>
        <MudText>
            Press <strong>Calculate</strong>, then look at the <em>Turn 4</em> row and the
            <em>≥4 lands</em> column — this is your probability of making the 4th land drop on time.
            The <em>Miss land drop</em> column in the same row shows the complementary risk.
        </MudText>
    </MudExpansionPanel>
</MudExpansionPanels>

<MudGrid>
    <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
        <MudCard Elevation="2">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Parameters</MudText>
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_deckSize" Label="Deck Size" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="1" Max="999" HelperText="Total cards in your deck" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_landCount" Label="Lands in Deck" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="0" Max="@_deckSize" HelperText="Number of land cards in your deck" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_handSize" Label="Opening Hand Size" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="1" Max="@_deckSize" HelperText="Cards in opening hand (default 7)" Class="mb-4" />
                <MudNumericField @bind-Value="_maxTurns" Label="Turns to Show" Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                    Min="1" Max="20" HelperText="Number of turns to display" />
            </MudCardContent>
            <MudCardActions Class="flex-column px-4 pb-4 pt-0">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" OnClick="Calculate" FullWidth="true"
                    StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Calculate" Class="mb-2">
                    Calculate
                </MudButton>
                <MudTooltip Text="Resets Deck Size, Hand Size, and Lands in Deck to format defaults — 24 lands for 60-card Traditional, 37 for 100-card Singleton, and 17 for 40-card Limited. Clears the current results.">
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" OnClick="ResetToFormat" FullWidth="true"
                        StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.RestartAlt">
                        Reset to chosen format
                    </MudButton>
                </MudTooltip>
            </MudCardActions>
        </MudCard>
    </MudItem>

    <MudItem xs="12" md="8">
        <MudCard Elevation="2" Class="mb-4">
            <MudCardHeader>
                <CardHeaderContent>
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Land Drop Probability by Turn</MudText>
                    @if (_calculated)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary">
                            @_landCount lands in @_deckSize cards — probability of seeing at least N lands
                        </MudText>
                    }
                </CardHeaderContent>
            </MudCardHeader>
            <MudCardContent>
                @if (_calculated)
                {
                    <PlotlyChart @ref="_chart" Config="_chartConfig" Layout="_chartLayout" Data="_chartData" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudPaper Class="d-flex align-center justify-center" Style="height:300px;" Elevation="0">
                        <MudText Color="Color.Secondary">Press Calculate to see the chart.</MudText>
                    </MudPaper>
                }
            </MudCardContent>
        </MudCard>

        @if (_calculated)
        {
            <MudCard Elevation="2">
                <MudCardHeader>
                    <CardHeaderContent>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Probability Table</MudText>
                    </CardHeaderContent>
                </MudCardHeader>
                <MudCardContent Class="pa-0">
                    <MudTable Items="_tableRows" Dense="true" Hover="true" Striped="true">
                        <HeaderContent>
                            <MudTh>Turn</MudTh>
                            <MudTh>Cards Seen</MudTh>
                            @for (int threshold = 1; threshold <= MaxThreshold; threshold++)
                            {
                                var t = threshold;
                                <MudTh>≥@t land@(t == 1 ? "" : "s")</MudTh>
                            }
                            <MudTh>Miss land drop</MudTh>
                        </HeaderContent>
                        <RowTemplate>
                            <MudTd>@(context.Turn == 0 ? "Opening hand" : $"Turn {context.Turn}")</MudTd>
                            <MudTd>@context.CardsSeen</MudTd>
                            @for (int threshold = 1; threshold <= MaxThreshold; threshold++)
                            {
                                var t = threshold;
                                <MudTd>@context.Probabilities[t - 1].ToString("P1")</MudTd>
                            }
                            <MudTd>@(context.MissLandDropProbability.HasValue ? context.MissLandDropProbability.Value.ToString("P1") : "—")</MudTd>
                        </RowTemplate>
                    </MudTable>
                </MudCardContent>
            </MudCard>
        }
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>
